  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\nHigh pressure sinks into the region this afternoon and kicks \noff a stretch of dry weather expected to last through the \nweekend. \n\nA ridge currently located in the western CONUS will begin a \nslow march eastward today. Heights rise locally beginning this \nweekend as the ridge slides into the central CONUS. This \ncontinues our dry weather and kicks off a warming trend that \nsees temperatures rise back above normal. By early next week \nthe ridge will continue moving eastward and become centered \nsomewhere across the southeast US. Our proximity to this ridge \nwill help push daytime highs back towards and into the low 90s.\nThis brings with it a likely moderate and possible major Heat \nRisk across the region peaking on Tuesday. Heat Risk will be \nhighest in urban centers and along the river valleys. The ridge \nis expected to begin to break down some by midweek as a series \nof shortwaves round and flatten the top of it. Most ensembles \nagree on a corresponding lowering of local heights by mid-to- \nlate next week, trimming high temperatures and heat risk back \nwith it.\n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...\nEnsembles hint at the return of showers and storm chances by \nnext week but differ on their timing and presentation of the \nthreat. The placement of our early week upper ridge is very \nimportant in both the timing and degree of storm coverage \nthrough next week. \n\nBy midweek, there is rather good agreement that a trough or \nseries of shortwaves cross the central CONUS and flatten the \nridge in the east. The favored storm track will be along the \nnortheastern periphery of the ridge. If the ridge stalls \ndirectly overhead, appreciable storm chances plummet as the \nfavored storm track sets up to our northeast across NY and New \nEngland. If the ridge stalls a little to our west then this \nfavored storm track settles overhead bringing rounds of active \nweather to the region during the heart of the next work week. \nMachine learning indicates some kind of broad severe risk across\nmuch of the Mid-Atlantic into the northeast by next Wednesday \nbut the finer details of this will largely depend on our \nimpending synoptic pattern this weekend, particularly where the \nridge sets up.",
